From 6d342a172085bd61780e5376a5dabc00d0ea471c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: friedger <mail@friedger.de>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:36:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(belfry): participant keys derived from a custody seed

Decision of 2026-10-24: participant keys are recoverable from one custody
seed plus Odoo.

- With KEYCAST_CUSTODY_SEED_FILE (64 hex characters, kept in memory on the
  VM and unlocked by a steward with a YubiKey), preload-user creates the
  key as HKDF-SHA256(salt "belfry/custody/v1", IKM = seed,
  info "belfry/nostr/v1/<vine_id>/<version>"), version from the request
  (key_version, default 0). The file is read on every use; a configured
  but missing seed answers 503 instead of creating an unrecoverable random
  key. Unset: random keys as upstream.
- preload-user with pubkey: recreates an account whose participant holds
  their own key (recovery after a self-custody move), without a key.
- Self-custody: with a custody seed, "keep this key" is refused (Belfry can
  recompute it); the security page asks for a new key.
